Track 1: Chrysalis Displacement
- Story & Context: In the mouth of the Ojo del Glaciar, a moth emerges from a frozen shell only to find its wings calcified by the rapid shift in ambient pressure. The percussion mimics the erratic twitching of the insect’s thorax against the ice, while the lead synth mourns the creature’s inability to reach the sun. "You are just a splinter in the skin of the frost," the vocal whispers, barely audible over the crackling mountain silence.
