Track 2: ¿Quién fracturó el silencio?
- Story & Context: Deep within the subterranean tunnels, Iara discovers her mentor—the legendary sound-cartographer Mateo—staring at a pool of meltwater where the surface tension is vibrating in perfect sync with his own heartbeat. The atmosphere thickens as she asks him why the glacier began to scream in a major key at exactly midnight, realizing he has been feeding the cave its own recording. "My mouth is a flooded valley," she confesses, her voice dripping with the heavy, liquid reverb of the cave walls.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A silhouette of a woman standing by a perfectly still, pitch-black underground lake, casting a long shadow toward an opening that reveals a towering wall of ancient, veined ice.

Track 3: The Metamorphosis of Sub-Zero 
- Story & Context: The final collapse of the central chamber forces the remnants of the dance circle to abandon their instruments and march toward the mountain's peak. Legend says they did not die but became part of the migration of the glacier, their physical forms shifting into the very mineral veins that feed the valley below. The beat becomes a relentless, tectonic stomp, burying the memory of the concert in a layer of permanent silt. "We return to the flow, and the flow has no name," chants the chorus as the instrumentation dissolves into pure white noise.
